    "independent 66-byte binary Note vector from original OS install/edit/export",
    "source bytes preserved; arbitrary extension; raw high bytes; all standard escapes; unknown and out-of-range escape handling",
    "empty Note and 20-bit length overflow boundary",
    "changed Wire length and aggregate byte totals after local-read retry; remote retry reuses packed bytes",
    "per-file error metadata survives Worker/controller; retry/next-file clears prior translation",
    "lost S/D/B ACKs recover before sender retransmission, exactly one file committed",
    "partial write starts ACK timer only on complete frame; next packet/command supersedes unsent stale ACK",
    "bounded silent peer and cancellation/reset isolation; original final-ACK grace expiry",
    "generic Kermit checksum corruption, lost ACK, duplicate data and sequence wrap tests",
    "Blocked final ACK expires without late output, even if transport never accepted its first byte"
